# LLM-Assisted Text Classification via Majority Voting — Free (Ollama) Edition

This repo runs **locally for free** using **Ollama** on macOS/Linux/Windows (no API keys).
Majority-vote baseline, early stopping, abstention, English + Arabic (LABR).

## 0) Install Ollama and a model
```bash
# macOS:
brew install ollama
ollama serve &                      # starts http://localhost:11434
# Pull a small model first (fast, low memory)
ollama pull llama3.2:3b-instruct
# Optional: stronger but heavier
# ollama pull deepseek-r1:7b
```

## 1) Install Python deps
```bash
pip install -e .
```

## 2) Quick run (free, local)
```bash
python -m scripts.eval_dataset --provider ollama --model llama3.2:3b-instruct \
  --dataset ag_news --k 3 --max-samples 50 --early-stop
```

## 3) Arabic LABR
Place a CSV at `data/labr_binary_test.csv` with columns: `text,label`  (labels: `Positive` or `Negative`), then:
```bash
python -m scripts.eval_dataset --provider ollama --model llama3.2:3b-instruct \
  --dataset labr --k 3 --max-samples 200
```

## 4) Optional (paid): OpenAI
If you later want to compare against GPT-4/GPT-4o, change `--provider openai` and set your `OPENAI_API_KEY`.

## Notes
- The prompt forces a single-label output; the voter ignores off-list outputs.
- Use `--abstain 0.8` for high-precision mode; `--early-stop` to save time at higher K.


# 0) Install Ollama + a small model
brew install ollama
ollama serve &
ollama pull llama3.2:3b-instruct

# 1) Install Python deps
pip install -e .

# 2) Run a free local experiment
python -m scripts.eval_dataset --provider ollama --model llama3.2:3b-instruct \
  --dataset ag_news --k 3 --max-samples 50 --early-stop

  ollama pull deepseek-r1:7b
python -m scripts.eval_dataset --provider ollama --model deepseek-r1:7b \
  --dataset ag_news --k 3 --max-samples 50
